# Milestone: M6
# Covers: Phase 3 Object root C-native methods.
#
# Verifies setSlot / getSlot / hasSlot / removeSlot / clone /
# addProto end-to-end via the realm-global Object proto.  Each
# method is a UClosure with native_fn != NULL installed by the
# stdlib boot (urbi_stdlib_boot → urbi_object_root_register).
#
# The atom-clone short-circuit (S-atom-clone-perf) is exercised by
# the `1.clone()` line: clone short-circuits for any non-UVAL_OBJECT
# receiver so 1.clone() yields the integer 1 with zero UObject
# allocation.
#
# Each REPL line is one expression whose final value frames; we use
# `;` to chain assignment + setup off the same line so the only
# framed value is the one we want to assert.

var o = Object.clone(); o.setSlot("x", 42); o.getSlot("x")
[00000000] 42

var o2 = Object.clone(); o2.setSlot("x", 42); o2.hasSlot("x")
[00000001] true

var o3 = Object.clone(); o3.hasSlot("missing")
[00000002] false

var o4 = Object.clone(); o4.setSlot("x", 1); o4.removeSlot("x"); o4.hasSlot("x")
[00000003] false

# Clone-of-int returns the int directly (S-atom-clone-perf).
1.clone()
[00000004] 1

# Clone-of-object allocates fresh; parent and clone are independent.
var p = Object.clone(); p.setSlot("v", 100); var c = p.clone(); c.setSlot("v", 200); p.v
[00000005] 100

var p2 = Object.clone(); p2.setSlot("v", 100); var c2 = p2.clone(); c2.setSlot("v", 200); c2.v
[00000006] 200
